     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:15px\">How can I specify the </span><code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);white-space:pre-wrap;color:rgb(36,39,41)\">re.form</code><span style=\"color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:15px\"> equation given as an argument to </span><code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);white-space:pre-wrap;color:rgb(36,39,41)\">posterior_predict{rstanarm}</code><span style=\"color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:15px\"> (or to </span><code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);white-space:pre-wrap;color:rgb(36,39,41)\">predict.merMod{lme4})</code><span style=\"color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:15px\"> in a two level-model for which I want to condition on one level but not the other? Thanks.</span><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "aDW9cBFTBAAJ",
   "from": "Ben Goodrich",
   "author": "743bbacc59f4b25f",
   "date": "2017-03-13T15:26:53Z",
   "subject": "Re: re.form equation",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">On Monday, March 13, 2017 at 11:01:59 AM UTC-4, John Palmer wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:15px\">How can I specify the </span><code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);white-space:pre-wrap;color:rgb(36,39,41)\">re.form</code><span style=\"color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:15px\"> equation given as an argument to </span><code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);white-space:pre-wrap;color:rgb(36,39,41)\">posterior_predict{rstanarm}</code><span style=\"color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:15px\"> (or to </span><code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);white-space:pre-wrap;color:rgb(36,39,41)\">predict.merMod{lme4})</code><span style=\"color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:15px\"> in a two level-model for which I want to condition on one level but not the other? Thanks.</span></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>That is supposed to work the same way in posterior_predict() as it does in predict.merMod(). I believe you just do something like <br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>where g is the grouping variable you want to condition on and you omit the grouping variable that you want to integrate over.<br><br>Ben <br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
