or which I want to condition on one level but not the other? Thanks.</span></div></blockquote><div><br>That is supposed to work the same way in posterior_predict() as it does in predict.merMod(). I believe you just do something like <br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>where g is the grouping variable you want to condition on and you omit the grouping variable that you want to integrate over.<br><br>Ben <br></div></div></blockquote></div>"
